# Project-local npm registry pin.
#
# Per bead work9flow-azy (dsh-A.10g, P1, foundation policy): the
# runtime/dsh-bridge sub-package depends on @deepseek-ai/dsh-sdk-*
# (0.1.1-rc.2), which carries shell/filesystem capabilities via the
# spawned dsh-jsonrpc-agent subprocess. Such dependencies MUST NOT
# silently swap across registries depending on whatever ~/.npmrc the
# operator happens to have set. We pin the canonical registry here so
# a fresh `npm install` from this directory is reproducible.
#
# This overrides ~/.npmrc only inside runtime/dsh-bridge/. To check:
#   cd runtime/dsh-bridge && npm config get registry
#   # → https://registry.npmjs.org/
#
# Note: this file does NOT regenerate package-lock.json — the existing
# lockfile's `resolved` URLs may still point at whichever registry the
# last `npm install` used. Future `npm install` runs from this directory
# will rewrite those URLs to canonical. That regeneration, if needed,
# is tracked separately.

registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
